From 8bd277c9f93770f2e597399fefa79310c78247a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mauri de Souza Meneguzzo <mauri870@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 10:24:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: add HDMI 2.1 FRL support

Add support for HDMI 2.1 Fixed Rate Link (FRL) on AMD display hardware,
enabling bandwidth up to 48 Gbps across four lanes. This allows HDMI 2.1
monitors to run at high refresh rates (e.g., 4K@144Hz) instead of being
limited to HDMI 2.0 TMDS bandwidth.

Key changes:

- amdgpu_dm_helpers.c: populate edid_caps.frl_caps (max_rate,
  max_rate_per_lane, max_lanes) from connector display_info in addition
  to the flat max_frl_rate field, so dc_stream.c signal upgrade logic
  has non-zero frl_caps.max_rate to act on.

- amdgpu_dm.c: include SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL in the freesync/VRR
  capability detection branch so HDMI Forum VRR is correctly reported
  when the sink negotiates FRL instead of TMDS.

- dc/resource/dcn35,dcn351,dcn36: add compat defines aliasing the
  DCN35+ renamed FIFO_PIXEL_ENCODING_TYPE register fields back to the
  FIFO_PIXEL_ENCODING names expected by the HPO HDMI stream encoder.

- dc/dccg/dcn35: add forward declaration for
  dccg35_disable_hdmistreamclk to fix ordering dependency.

- dc/hpo/dcn30/dcn30_hpo_hdmi_stream_encoder.c: resolve struct
  frl_audio_clock_info conflict by using a local struct with a
  frl_lane_rate field and copying fields individually.

- dc/link/protocols/link_hdmi_frl: add hdmi_decide_link_settings
  wrapper expected by dc_resource.c.

- dc/dml2_0/dml21: remove duplicate SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL case.
